{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218620,"nonce":"wJQfdFn3/p3L8nwuCYhbr3I2MRk=","title":"convert_type recursed forever on a type holding its own kind","message":"`@reference struct Node { left: Node, right: Node, item: i64 }` ran\nthe compiler out of stack. Both copies of convert_type, in ssa.rs and\nlowering.rs, expanded a struct's fields unconditionally. Every linked\nstructure in the language was unwritable, which is why the allocation\nbenchmark had been written with raw pointers and hand-computed offsets.\n\nFixed with an in-progress set per builder: re-entering a type carries\nthe name alone. A read through such a field re-expands the name where\na layout is needed (SsaBuilder::struct_body). Both copies must be fixed\ntogether; fixing one moves the overflow into the other.","files":null}]}